--TEST--
a double-quoted string reads a variable written inside it, so the cursor inside one is offered the variables in scope and no reserved word or type, because the text is not a statement, `rule:ide/completion-offers-only-what-the-compiler-derived`
--FILE--
<?nvs
string $name = "world";
echo "he<|>llo";
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
$name   variable  string
